{"name":"Power Outage","hex":"#332244","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"power outage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A power cut"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/power_outage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Power outage","blocks":[{"text":"A power outage, also called a blackout, a power failure, a power blackout, a power loss, a power cut, a power out or a power drought is the complete loss of the electrical power network supply to an end user."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Calle_Larga_at_night_during_power_cut.jpg/330px-Calle_Larga_at_night_during_power_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_outage"},{"title":"Charmed season 3","blocks":[{"text":"The third season of Charmed, an American supernatural drama television series created by Constance M. Burge, originally aired in the United States on The WB from October 5, 2000, through May 17, 2001. Paramount Home Entertainment released the complete third season in a six-disc box set on November 15, 2005. It was later released on high-definition blu-ray on May 18, 2021."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/42/Charmed_%28season_3%29_DVD_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charmed_season_3"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Crossed_wires.JPG/500px-Crossed_wires.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Crossed_wires.JPG/500px-Crossed_wires.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tree limbs creating a short circuit in power lines during a storm on July 21, 2006. This typically results in a power outage in the area supplied by these lines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o